      "title": "Assistant Director for Programming, Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Stetson University - Career Opportunities | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Director for Programming, Alumni Engagement (AS6476) | . page has loaded. Assistant Director for Programming, Alumni Engagement (AS6476) | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Stetson University - Career Opportunities Menu Stetson University - Career Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Director for Programming, Alumni Engagement (AS6476) Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Director for Programming, Alumni Engagement (AS6476) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location DeLand, FL Job Type Full-Time Staff Division Development & Alumni Engagement Department Office of Alumni Engagement Opening Date 07/24/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits Job Description **Position start date: September 1, 2026** Reporting to the Director of Alumni Engagement, the Assistant Director supports programming initiatives within the Development and Alumni Engagement Division. The Assistant Director plans, executes, and attends events for alumni, donors, students, and parents both on the DeLand campus and regionally across the country. Responsibilities include sourcing and managing vendors (venues, catering, rentals), overseeing attendee registration and event setup, and ensuring cost efficiency to deliver seamless events from start to finish. Essential Job Functions and Responsibilities: Employment duties include, but are not limited to: Plan and manage in-person and virtual events for alumni, donors, and campus partners that provide value, build alumni pride, and foster relationships and community. Develop meaningful and creative programming that engages alumni with the university and one another. Provide leadership, support, and direction to volunteers and program participants. Manage event registration for all events, including on-site registration for Homecoming and other large flagship events within the Development and Alumni Engagement Division. Utilize the university's CRM and event platforms to generate invitation lists, create RSVP forms, and report attendance data to event hosts and participating staff. Collaborate with the alumni team and campus partners to coordinate event setup and programming, including room reservations, catering, and audiovisual needs. Partner with Donor Relations on donor-specific event logistics as needed, including the management of athletic suites during the fall and spring semesters. Collaborate with Academic Deans to support alumni events within their colleges and schools, including the annual Joint Board Meeting, and provide event support as needed. Work with colleagues in Campus Life and Student Success to plan alumni engagement opportunities during Family and Friends Weekend, FOCUS, and Commencement that highlight Legacy students and families. Plan home and away tailgates for alumni and parents in support of university athletic teams as needed. Conduct post-event evaluations and prepare reports documenting outcomes, opportunities, challenges, and recommendations for future improvements. Attend events, board meetings, and other functions as needed. This position may require travel and work outside normal business hours. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: The Assistant Director will demonstrate: Strategic thinking combined with strong attention to detail and goal orientation. Proven ability to build relationships and collaborate effectively with a wide range of university constituents. Ability to meet deadlines, work independently and under pressure, and manage multiple projects simultaneously. Excellent interpersonal, written, verbal, and organizational skills. High energy, initiative, and self-motivation. A strong commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion, demonstrated through building and supporting community. Proficiency in the Microsoft Office Suite. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or two (2) years of relevant professional experience. Ideal Candidate Qualifications : The ideal candidate will have: Experience developing and implementing programs. Experience working with volunteers. Experience planning and managing events. Work Environment: The work environment is lively and energetic. Daily operations are primarily office-based; however, events may take place indoors or outdoors and occasionally require work outside normal business hours. Pay Grade: 6 This position is benefit eligible. Stetson University offers a variety of benefits for our full-time employees including comprehensive Medical, Dental, and Vision insurance, employer paid life and disability insurance, generous leave and holiday benefits, employer retirement contributions, tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, and others. All employees are also eligible to enjoy our Hatter Perks which include a variety of discounts and special privileges within our community. Please visit our employee benefits webpage for more information. Employer Stetson University Division Development & Alumni Engagement Address 421 N. Woodland Blvd. DeLand, Florida, 32723 Phone 386-822-8710 Website https://www.stetson.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Stetson University - Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. . Stetson University - Career Opportunities Menu Close Menu . Stetson University - Career Opportunities Email Job Alerts Stetson University (DeLand) Steston College of Law (Gulfport) People Ops/HR Instagram Help & Support Translate SOCIAL Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled