      "title": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid, Funded Scholarships",
      "description": "Stetson University - Career Opportunities | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Director of Financial Aid, Funded Scholarships (AS6497) | . page has loaded. Assistant Director of Financial Aid, Funded Scholarships (AS6497) | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Stetson University - Career Opportunities Menu Stetson University - Career Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Director of Financial Aid, Funded Scholarships (AS6497) Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Director of Financial Aid, Funded Scholarships (AS6497) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location DeLand, FL Job Type Full-Time Staff Division Enrollment Management & Marketing Department Student Financial Planning - DeLand Opening Date 08/02/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits Job Description The Assistant Director of Financial Aid, Funded Scholarships supports Stetson University by strategically administering endowed and annual (current-use) scholarship funds that expand access to higher education and reduce financial barriers for students. Serving as a member of the Office of Student Financial Planning team, this position is responsible for the administration, allocation, reconciliation, and compliance of donor-funded scholarship programs while ensuring awards align with donor intent and applicable regulations. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Enrollment Management/Executive Director of Financial Aid and working closely with the Vice President of Enrollment Management and campus partners, the Assistant Director supports the University's goal of meeting 100% of demonstrated financial need through the effective stewardship and utilization of scholarship resources. This position serves as a key liaison among Enrollment Management, Advancement, Development, academic departments, and scholarship program administrators to ensure scholarship funding is awarded strategically, accurately, and in accordance with established guidelines. In alignment with Stetson's Strategic Priorities, the Assistant Director of Financial Aid – Funded Scholarships helps create educational access and student success opportunities by leveraging donor-funded resources, supporting recruitment and retention efforts, and promoting student financial wellness. Essential Job Functions and Responsibilities Employment duties include, but are not limited to: Scholarship Administration and Compliance Serve as the primary administrator for endowed and annual scholarship funds. Review scholarship candidate profiles for accuracy and alignment with donor specifications, eligibility criteria, and donor intent. Award scholarship funds in compliance with donor agreements, institutional policies, and applicable regulations. Ensure effective utilization of available scholarship resources to support enrollment and student success goals. Review and interpret scholarship agreements and funding requirements to ensure accurate award administration. Financial Analysis, Reconciliation, and Reporting Reconcile and analyze scholarship funding reports to ensure all available funds are utilized strategically and responsibly. Conduct regular reconciliation of scholarship awards between Banner and Scholarship Manager. Monitor scholarship balances and spending activity to ensure compliance and maximize funding opportunities. Prepare and review reports related to scholarship allocations, utilization, and fund availability. Collaboration and Partnership Management Serve as a liaison between Enrollment Management and university departments requesting scholarship awards, including affiliated foundations and academic units. Determine student eligibility and feasibility of scholarship requests within financial aid award packages. Collaborate with Advancement and Development to maintain the accuracy and integrity of scholarship data. Coordinate the implementation of new scholarship funds and ensure alignment between Scholarship Manager and Banner account structures. Scholarship Program Support Partner with Stetson University's premier scholarship programs, including programs such as JOE and other institutional scholarship initiatives. Support the notification, awarding, and administration of scholarship recipients while ensuring program-specific requirements are met. Coordinate with campus stakeholders to provide consistent administration and communication regarding scholarship opportunities. Student Outreach and Financial Literacy Conduct outreach initiatives and educational programs that promote scholarship awareness and financial literacy. Assist students in identifying and accessing scholarship resources to support educational funding. Participate in recruitment and retention initiatives focused on removing financial barriers to persistence and graduation. Serve as an active member of the University's Retention Task Force Committee. Customer Service and Student Support Provide accurate and timely financial aid information to students, families, and campus constituents. Respond to inquiries via telephone, email, virtual meeting platforms, and in-person appointments. Maintain a high level of customer service while working in a fast-paced, high-volume environment. Additional Responsibilities Participate in occasional evening and weekend activities as needed. Perform other site- and position-specific duties as assigned. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The knowledge, skills, and abilities for this role include: Thorough knowledge of federal and state financial aid programs, regulations, and compliance requirements. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to interpret financial and enrollment data. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong customer service skills and ability to work effectively with students, families, faculty, and staff. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced, high-volume environment. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Word, Excel, and Outlook. Ability to reconcile complex financial data and maintain accurate records. Ability to work independently and collaboratively across departments. Commitment to confidentiality, sound judgment, and ethical administration of student financial aid resources. Support the University's Mission and Values through a commitment to student success, inclusive excellence, and collaborative service. Required Qualifications This position requires: Bachelor's degree. Minimum of three (3) years of student financial aid experience. Experience interpreting and applying federal and state financial aid regulations. Experience utilizing student information systems, databases, or financial aid management systems. Strong computer proficiency, including Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook. Desire to join a distinct university community committed to inclusive excellence, kindness, and collaboration, as it seeks to move Forward Together in making our community and world a better place. Ideal Candidate Qualifications The ideal candidate's qualifications include: Master's degree. Experience with Banner and Slate. Experience with Scholarship Manager or similar scholarship administration software. Experience administering donor-funded, endowed, or institutional scholarship programs. Experience with scholarship fund reconciliation and financial reporting. Experience supporting student retention and enrollment management initiatives. Experience conducting financial literacy programming and student outreach. Knowledge of higher education enrollment management practices and scholarship leveraging strategies. Work Environment Work is primarily performed in a professional office environment. The tasks involved in this position are generally sedentary in nature and regularly performed without exposure to adverse environmental conditions. Responsibilities may require occasional walking, bending, light lifting, and travel to meetings or university events. The position may require occasional evening and weekend hours to support departmental and university initiatives. Pay Grade: 6 Work authorization sponsorship may be available for this position. However, sponsorship is contingent upon the non-applicability of the visa petition fees outlined in the relevant Executive Order signed September 19, 2025. Due to the recent federally-mandated increased financial expense, the university is not in a position to absorb this significantly increased cost of sponsorship for new H-1B petitions at this time. International candidates are encouraged to apply, but should be aware that eligibility for sponsorship will be evaluated in accordance with current U.S. immigration regulations and institutional policies. This position is benefit eligible. Stetson University offers a variety of benefits for our full-time employees including comprehensive Medical, Dental, and Vision insurance, employer paid life and disability insurance, generous leave and holiday benefits, employer retirement contributions, tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, and others. All employees are also eligible to enjoy our Hatter Perks which include a variety of discounts and special privileges within our community. Please visit our employee benefits webpage for more information. Employer Stetson University Division Enrollment Management & Marketing Address 421 N. Woodland Blvd. DeLand, Florida, 32723 Phone 386-822-8710 Website https://www.stetson.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Stetson University - Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are