06/10/2026 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits Questions Job Description Position Summary: The Senior Graphic Designer plays a crucial role within our integrated marketing department's Creative Services team, focusing on digital and print design projects to enhance Stetson University's visibility. This role demands strong conceptual skills and a solid design foundation to ensure timely, compelling, and brand-aligned creative that supports our marketing objectives. Essential Job Functions and Responsibilities: Develop and execute concepts for marketing, fundraising and advertising initiatives. Translate creative ideas into cohesive print and digital media solutions, maintaining consistency across platforms. Provide project leadership under the guidance of the Art Director, collaborating across departments as a design expert in digital, print, and social media. Lead and manage creative projects from inception to delivery, ensuring adherence to timelines and effective presentation of conceptual ideas to stakeholders. Champion the institutional brand through consistent application of identity standards across all media channels. Stay current with design trends and standards, integrating them into digital and print graphic design. Collaborate effectively within the creative department, communications, and web teams. Contribute positively to group creative discussions and work well in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong communication skills with a deep understanding of advertising principles, design best practices, typography, media trends, and print production. Expertise in Adobe Creative Suite and Mac platform, with proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite. Adobe Premiere and/or Final Cut are a plus. Ability to multitask in a deadline-driven environment while maintaining focus on strategic and timeline objectives. Proficiency in both raster and vector-based graphics, including photo editing and illustration. The strongest candidates for the Senior Graphic Designer position will also have solid multimedia skills. While this is primarily a graphic design position, duties will also include occasionally supporting the staff photographer/videographer to cover university events and other photo/video requests as needed. Candidates with this skillset must be able to produce high quality photos and videos, and have solid photo/video editing skills. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in graphic design or related field. Minimum five (5) years of graphic design and/or art direction experience in an agency or in-house marketing setting. Strong portfolio demonstrating creative and technical skills across various media platforms. Work Environment: This is an on-site position at our DeLand campus. Our Marketing division operates in an open-air indoor environment with 20-30 employees. Noise levels vary but are generally moderate. Pay Grade: 7 Work authorization sponsorship may be available for this position. However, sponsorship is contingent upon the non-applicability of the visa petition fees outlined in the relevant Executive Order signed September 19, 2025. Due to the recent federally-mandated increased financial expense, the university is not in a position to absorb this significantly increased cost of sponsorship for new H-1B petitions at this time. International candidates are encouraged to apply, but should be aware that eligibility for sponsorship will be evaluated in accordance with current U.S. immigration regulations and institutional policies. This position is benefit eligible. Stetson University offers a variety of benefits for our full-time employees including comprehensive Medical, Dental, and Vision insurance, employer paid life and disability insurance, generous leave and holiday benefits, employer retirement contributions, tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, and others. All employees are also eligible to enjoy our Hatter Perks which include a variety of discounts and special privileges within our community. Please visit our employee benefits webpage for more information. 01 What are your salary expectations? 02 Do you have any of the following experience or expertise? Photography, Videography, Storytelling Required Question Employer Stetson University Division Enrollment Management & Marketing Address 421 N. Woodland Blvd. DeLand, Florida, 32723 Phone 386-822-8710 Website https://www.stetson.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Stetson University - Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    