      "title": "Senior Director of Development",
      "description": "Stetson University - Career Opportunities | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Senior Director of Development (AS6468) | . page has loaded. Senior Director of Development (AS6468) | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Stetson University - Career Opportunities Menu Stetson University - Career Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Senior Director of Development (AS6468) Print Apply ﻿ Senior Director of Development (AS6468) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location DeLand, FL Job Type Full-Time Staff Remote Employment Flexible/Hybrid Division Development & Alumni Engagement Department Development Program-Deland Opening Date 07/27/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A -- Pay Grade: 10 Description Benefits Job Description The Senior Director of Development is a highly experienced, strategic fundraising professional responsible for managing a portfolio of major and principal gift prospects and donors ($50,000+ with an emphasis on $100,000+ and above). This results-oriented and relationship-driven leader will identify, cultivate, solicit, negotiate, and steward gift commitments from Stetson alumni and friends in support of university-wide and college/unit priorities. The Senior Director will serve as a key partner to university leadership, including deans, senior administrators, and the Assistant Vice President of Development, providing strategic direction on fundraising initiatives, campaign priorities, and donor engagement. This position will also play a leadership role within the Development (Major Gifts) team, mentoring colleagues and helping to drive the overall advancement strategy. The position is based in DeLand and carries a regional and/or national portfolio. In alignment with Stetson's Strategic Priorities, the Senior Director of Development promotes a relationship-rich culture of philanthropy, strengthens donor engagement, and advances the university's ability to provide transformative educational experiences through philanthropic investment. Start Date: September 1, 2026 Essential Job Functions and Responsibilities: Employment duties include, but are not limited to: Develop and execute comprehensive fundraising strategies in partnership with deans, faculty, senior administrators, and advancement leadership. Manage a portfolio of high-capacity prospects and donors with an emphasis on leadership, major, and principal gift opportunities. Identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit, negotiate, and steward donors through highly personalized engagement strategies. Secure philanthropic commitments of $50,000 and above, with a focus on six- and seven-figure gifts. Lead the development of complex proposals, gift agreements, naming opportunities, and multi-year funding strategies aligned with university priorities. Provide strategic counsel to university leadership regarding donor engagement opportunities, fundraising trends, campaign priorities, and philanthropic initiatives. Collaborate across Development and Alumni Engagement teams to strengthen prospect pipeline development, campaign performance, and donor engagement efforts. Mentor and support development colleagues and contribute to a high-performing, collaborative team environment. Prepare and present strategic donor briefings for senior leadership, volunteers, and key stakeholders. Maintain accurate donor and prospect records, contact reports, fundraising plans, and performance metrics using Raiser's Edge NXT or a similar CRM platform. Track portfolio activity, pipeline development, fundraising outcomes, and progress toward established goals. Represent the university at fundraising events, donor meetings, and institutional engagements, including evenings and weekends as needed. Travel extensively throughout assigned regions and nationally to cultivate and solicit donor relationships. Perform occasional physical activities including standing, walking, light lifting of materials and equipment (4-20 lbs.), and prolonged periods working at a computer. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: The knowledge, skills, and abilities for this role include: Extensive knowledge of fundraising principles, donor relations, advancement ethics, and campaign strategy. Demonstrated ability to build meaningful relationships and secure significant philanthropic investments. Strong strategic planning and analytical skills with the ability to develop and execute complex fundraising strategies. Excellent interpersonal, verbal, presentation, and written communication skills. Ability to influence, collaborate, and build trust with donors, volunteers, faculty, administrators, and other stakeholders. Ability to exercise discretion and maintain confidentiality regarding donor information and institutional priorities. Proven project management, organizational, and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. Strong problem-solving abilities and sound professional judgment. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and donor database/CRM systems, preferably Raiser's Edge NXT. Commitment to donor-centered fundraising practices and exceptional customer service. Support the University's Mission and Values in their role. Required Qualifications: This position requires: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. Minimum of eight (8) to ten (10) years of progressively responsible experience in higher education fundraising, nonprofit development, advancement, philanthropy, or a related client-facing/sales profession. Demonstrated success securing and closing major gifts of $50,000 or greater. Proven ability to manage a portfolio of prospects and donors through all stages of the fundraising cycle. Ability to travel extensively and maintain a valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Desire to join a distinct university community committed to inclusive excellence, kindness, and collaboration, as it seeks to move Forward Together in making our community and world a better place. Ideal Candidate Qualifications: The ideal candidate's qualifications include: Master's degree from an accredited institution. Significant fundraising experience within a college or university environment. Demonstrated success securing six- and seven-figure philanthropic commitments. Experience developing and implementing complex gift strategies including planned gifts, blended gifts, and multi-year commitments. Experience partnering directly with deans, senior administrators, advisory boards, and volunteer leadership. Proven leadership experience, including mentoring, coaching, or guiding development professionals. Experience supporting comprehensive fundraising campaigns and strategic advancement initiatives. Expertise with Raiser's Edge NXT and advancement analytics tools. Strong understanding of trends, best practices, and emerging opportunities in higher education philanthropy. Work Environment This position operates primarily in a professional office environment with frequent travel throughout assigned regions and nationally to meet with prospects and donors. The role requires regular use of standard office technology and extended periods of computer work. The position includes attendance at university events, donor engagements, and fundraising activities that may occur during evenings and weekends. Flexible work arrangements, including hybrid work options, may be available based on business needs and university guidelines. Because the primary territory for this role is Broward and Miami-Dade Counties, the university is open to hiring a candidate based in either county to support effective donor cultivation, engagement, and fundraising activities within the region. Pay Grade: 10 Work authorization sponsorship may be available for this position. However, sponsorship is contingent upon the non-applicability of the visa petition fees outlined in the relevant Executive Order signed September 19, 2025. Due to the recent federally-mandated increased financial expense, the university is not in a position to absorb this significantly increased cost of sponsorship for new H-1B petitions at this time. International candidates are encouraged to apply, but should be aware that eligibility for sponsorship will be evaluated in accordance with current U.S. immigration regulations and institutional policies. This position is benefit eligible. Stetson University offers a variety of benefits for our full-time employees including comprehensive Medical, Dental, and Vision insurance, employer paid life and disability insurance, generous leave and holiday benefits, employer retirement contributions, tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, and others. All employees are also eligible to enjoy our Hatter Perks which include a variety of discounts and special privileges within our community. Please visit our employee benefits webpage for more information. Employer Stetson University Division Development & Alumni Engagement Address 421 N. Woodland Blvd. DeLand, Florida, 32723 Phone 386-822-8710 Website https://www.stetson.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Stetson University - Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. . Stetson University - Career Opportunities Menu Close Menu . Stetson University - Career Opportunities Email Job Alerts Stetson University (DeLand) Steston College of Law (Gulfport) People Ops/HR Instagram Help & Support Translate SOCIAL Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled by Governmentjobs.com, Inc. (DBA “NEOGOV”), including our related brands NEOGOV.com, NEOED.com, PowerDMS.com, Governmentjobs.com, Schooljobs.com, and our mobile app(s) (collectively referred to as the “Services”), or affiliated companies (collectively referred to herein as “Governmentjobs”, \"Schooljobs\", “NEOGOV”, “NEOED”, “PowerDMS”, “we”, “us”, or “our”). By using any part of the Services you agree that you have read this Policy, your personal data will be processed as described herein, and you agree to be bound by this Policy. This Policy is incorporated into our Terms of Use . Definitions not explicitly defined herein shall retain the meaning as prescribed in the Terms of Use . Any dispute related to privacy is subject to the Terms of Use and this Policy, including limitations on liability. This Policy does not apply to (1) personal data controlled by our Customers (employers that utilize our Services, described further below), which is governed by our separate agreements and related data processing agreements with such Customers; (2) personal data collected by unaffiliated sites that link to or are accessible from our Services; (3) personal data our partners may collect directly from you and control; (4) personal data collected and processed by us about our employees or job applicants responding to our job offers; and, (5) non-personal data derived from personal data, including any data that is aggregated, de-identified, or anonymized, statistical data, insights, or other predictive data that is sufficiently different from your personal data that it cannot be reversed engineered through reasonable means, or otherwise identified from analysis or further processing of the derived data (collectively referred to as the “De-Identified Platform Data”). We use De-Identified Platform Data to provide Customers with useful and relevant insights, build features and data services, and improve our Services.  Because De-Identified Platform Data does not identify you personally, we can use and disclose it in our discretion. We are the controller for the personal data discussed in this Policy, except as noted in the “Where We Are a Service Provider” section below. Where We Are a Service Provider Our Customers are organizations such as federal, state, local, tribal, or other municipal government agencies (including administrative agencies, departments, and offices thereof), private businesses, and educational institutions (including without limitation K-12 schools, colleges, universities, and vocational schools), who use our Services to evaluate job applicants and/or manage their relationship with their personnel. When we provide our Services to our Customers, the Customer generally controls and manages the personal data (which may include sensitive personal data such as biometric information or your precise geolocation information for timeclock tracking, health information, and demographic information like race and ethnicity related to the employment relationship), and we process personal data as a \"data processor\" or \"service provider\" (as these terms are defined in applicable data protection laws). Any use of analytics or engagement technologies that process personal data, including tools that analyze user behavior or associate usage with identifiers, are implemented solely as a data processor or service provider in these scenarios, and such data is not used by NEOGOV for its own commercial purposes. Our legal obligations as a processor and service provider are set out in our Customer contracts and policies.  Our Customers, and not us, decide what types of personal data to collect to manage their relationships with you. For example, a Customer may choose to enable collection of biometric or precise location data for its employees using our time and attendance product. We process such data only at the direction of that Customer and do not use it for our own purposes. Further, if you apply to a job or your employer utilizes our Services to manage their relationship with you, the personal data collected about you is generally controlled by the employer (our Customer). This Policy does not describe the processing of your personal data by our Customers, and we encourage you to visit the Customer’s privacy policy for information about their privacy practices. For example, if you applied to a job at a local state agency, you should contact that agency with any questions you may have relating to the personal data processing by that state agency within our Services. Where we serve as a data processor or service provider, our Customer contracts and policies require us to either instruct you to contact our Customer, or redirect your inquiry to our Customer. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. In this Section we set out general categories of personal data we may collect and the purpose for using your personal data, including the personal data collected and processed over the past year. We collect and process personal data to provide you the Services, fulfill our contractual responsibility to deliver the Services to our Customers, fulfill your requests, and pursue our legitimate interests and our business and commercial purposes. We also automatically collect data during your usage of the Services and collect other personal data about you from other sources. Your personal data will only be collected and used for purposes stated herein, where you provide additional consent, or as required by law or regulation - including national security or law enforcement requirements. Information Provided by You. We collect personal data from you directly when you visit our Services from either your computer, mobile phone, or other device, attend one our events, or communicate with our personnel. The categories of personal data we collect from you, involve the following: Types of Personal Data Why the Personal Data is collected Identification, account, and contact data, including your name, username and password, professional or personal email address, professional or personal telephone phone number, and account"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stetson/jobs/5466320/pre-law-advisor-law-ready-associate-director-as9864": {
      "title": "Pre-Law Advisor/Law Ready Associate Director",
      "description": "Stetson University - Career Opportunities | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Pre-Law Advisor/Law Ready Associate Director (AS9864) | . page has loaded. Pre-Law Advisor/Law Ready Associate Director (AS9864) | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Stetson University - Career Opportunities Menu Stetson University - Career Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Pre-Law Advisor/Law Ready Associate Director (AS9864) Print Apply ﻿ Pre-Law Advisor/Law Ready Associate Director (AS9864) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location DeLand, FL Job Type Full-Time Staff Division Academic Affairs | College of Arts & Sciences Department Dean of School of Arts & Sciences Opening Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A -- Pay Grade: 06 Description Benefits Job Description The Pre-Law Advisor/Law Ready Associate Director works with the Law Ready Director to support Stetson University by designing and directing initiatives to promote the mission and goals of the Law Ready program. Serving as a member of the Law Ready Team within Academic Affairs, the Pre-Law Advisor/Law Ready Associate Director is the focal position responsible for designing and implementing all efforts to ensure success for students interested in a law-related career. Serves as the primary admissions counselor for Law Ready and as the central student advisor for all Law Ready students. Coordinates and manages student pre-law organizations. In alignment with Stetson’s Strategic Priorities , the Pre-Law Advisor/Law Ready Associate Director will design, implement, and advance programs that promote contemporary, integrative and engaged learning, as well as student success and well-being. Start Date: 10/1/2026 Essential Job Functions and Responsibilities: Serves as a Pre-Law Academic Advisor for undergraduate students in the Law Ready program. Provides guidance on the field of law, how to excel in the first year, exploring majors, engaging in experiential learning, and pathways to law school. Supports students by helping with LSAT readiness, law school application preparation (e.g., resumes, personal statements, and other writing samples), application timelines, potential school research, and assisting with law school financial planning. Maintains detailed advising notes in the University’s system and communicates, as needed, with students’ major academic advisor. Participates in pre-law information, outreach, and programming initiatives in coordination with the Law Ready Director. Assists with University-wide Advisor education programs. Participates in actively recruiting prospective students to the Law Ready program. Partners with Admissions to design novel and effective recruitment programming and materials. Attends and presents at University recruitment events and participates in individual meetings with prospective students and families. May involve some travel to off-campus recruitment events and related opportunities. Maintains websites and digital communications for Law Ready. Directs and manages the 4+3/3+3 Pathway Cohort program. Communicates and meets with students in these programs to ensure they are maintaining adequate progress to meet required benchmarks. Designs and implements additional student support programming to promote success. Actively recruits prospective and current students into these pathways. Coordinates with Stetson College of Law Admissions on updates to the program. Assists the Law Ready Director in all aspects related to the success of the Mock Trial and Moot Court teams. Serves as primary coordinator of team logistics, including student recruitment, coach recruitment and support, competition planning, travel coordination and budget management. Serves as the staff advisor for the Law Ready Executive Council. Helps coordinate and support the activities of all Pre-Law related student groups, including Mock Trial, Moot Court, Phi Alpha Theta, Black Law Student Association, and the LatinX Law Student Association. Partners with the Office of Institutional Research and Effectiveness to track, analyze and produce reports on key Law Ready metrics, including recruitment, student success, and post-graduation outcomes. Works with the Law Ready Director to organize annual events, such as Law Ready Orientation, Law Ready Homecoming event, and the Senior Decision Panel. Provides ongoing information and updates on law school admission trends relevant to Stetson students and the Law Ready program. Actively follows relevant changes to policies impacting students applying to law school. Attends conferences and workshops to maintain industry best practices. Collaborates with the Law Ready Director to advance initiatives that further the goals and mission of Law Ready. Performs other duties as assigned by the Dean of the College of Arts and Sciences. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to use University database systems to compile pertinent academic information and maintain confidentiality. Creative problem-solving skills. Experience with Microsoft Office and ability to learn other computing software systems. Ability to interpret and explain policies, procedures, goals, and objectives to students, parents, faculty, and staff. Ability to prioritize, organize, and complete multiple work assignments simultaneously with minimal supervision. Ability to deal with people in a calm, confident manner and with complete objectivity. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, parents, supervisors, and interdepartmental personnel. Attention to detail with a high standard of integrity. Support the University’s Mission and Values in their role. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university required; J.D. or related advanced degree strongly preferred. At least two years of experience in higher education setting working with students. Must possess current driver license and an insurable driving record through the University’s insurance provide. Desire to join a distinct university community committed to inclusive excellence, kindness, and collaboration, as it seeks to move Forward Together in making our community and world a better place. Ideal Candidate Qualifications: Experience in student academic advising, ideally with a pre-law focus. Experience in communicating with or working directly with law schools. Excellent presentation and communication skills with the ability to respond to questions in a group setting in a clear and thorough manner. Experience managing and supporting student groups and organizations. Knowledge of effective budget management practices. Ability to offer law-related courses to undergraduates when needed. Direct experience participating in or advising/coaching Mock Trial or Moot Court competitive teams. Work Environment: Work primarily in a professional office setting with frequent interaction with students, faculty, staff, and visitors. The position requires managing multiple priorities, maintaining confidentiality, and collaborating across academic departments. Occasional evening or weekend participation in student programs, recruitment activities, and special events may be required. Work authorization sponsorship may be available for this position. However, sponsorship is contingent upon the non-applicability of the visa petition fees outlined in the relevant Executive Order signed September 19, 2025. Due to the recent federally mandated increased financial expense, the university is not in a position to absorb this significantly increased cost of sponsorship for new H-1B petitions at this time. International candidates are encouraged to apply but should be aware that eligibility for sponsorship will be evaluated in accordance with current U.S. immigration regulations and institutional policies. This position is benefit eligible. Stetson University offers a variety of benefits for our full-time employees including comprehensive Medical, Dental, and Vision insurance, employer paid life and disability insurance, generous leave and holiday benefits, employer retirement contributions, tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, and others. All employees are also eligible to enjoy our Hatter Perks which include a variety of discounts and special privileges within our community. Please visit our employee benefits webpage for more information. Employer Stetson University Division Academic Affairs | College of Arts & Sciences Address 421 N. Woodland Blvd. DeLand, Florida, 32723 Phone 386-822-8710 Website https://www.stetson.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Stetson University - Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. . Stetson University - Career Opportunities Menu Close Menu . Stetson University - Career Opportunities Email Job Alerts Stetson University (DeLand) Steston College of Law (Gulfport) People Ops/HR Instagram Help & Support Translate SOCIAL Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled by Governmentjobs.com, Inc. (DBA “NEOGOV”), including our related brands NEOGOV.com, NEOED.com, PowerDMS.com, Governmentjobs.com, Schooljobs.com, and our mobile app(s) (collectively referred to as the “Services”), or affiliated companies (collectively referred to herein as “Governmentjobs”, \"Schooljobs\", “NEOGOV”, “NEOED”, “PowerDMS”, “we”, “us”, or “our”). By using any part of the Services you agree that you have read this Policy, your personal data will be processed as described herein, and you agree to be bound by this Policy. This Policy is incorporated into our Terms of Use . Definitions not explicitly defined herein shall retain the meaning as prescribed in the Terms of Use . Any dispute related to privacy is subject to the Terms of Use and this Policy, including limitations on liability. This Policy does not apply to (1) personal data controlled by our Customers (employers that utilize our Services, described further below), which is governed by our separate agreements and related data processing agreements with such Customers; (2) personal data collected by unaffiliated sites that link to or are accessible from our Services; (3) personal data our partners may collect directly from you and control; (4) personal data collected and processed by us about our employees or job applicants responding to our job offers; and, (5) non-personal data derived from personal data, including any data that is aggregated, de-identified, or anonymized, statistical data, insights, or other predictive data that is sufficiently different from your personal data that it cannot be reversed engineered through reasonable means, or otherwise identified from analysis or further processing of the derived data (collectively referred to as the “De-Identified Platform Data”). We use De-Identified Platform Data to provide Customers with useful and relevant insights, build features and data services, and improve our Services.  Because De-Identified Platform Data does not identify you personally, we can use and disclose it in our discretion. We are the controller for the personal data discussed in this Policy, except as noted in the “Where We Are a Service Provider” section below. Where We Are a Service Provider Our Customers are organizations such as federal, state, local, tribal, or other municipal government agencies (including administrative agencies, departments, and offices thereof), private businesses, and educational institutions (including without limitation K-12 schools, colleges, universities, and vocational schools), who use our Services to evaluate job applicants and/or manage their relationship with their personnel. When we provide our Services to our Customers, the Customer generally controls and manages the personal data (which may include sensitive personal data such as biometric information or your precise geolocation information for timeclock tracking, health information, and demographic information like race and ethnicity related to the employment relationship), and we process personal data as a \"data processor\" or \"service provider\" (as these terms are defined in applicable data protection laws). Any use of analytics or engagement technologies that process personal data, including tools that analyze user behavior or associate usage with identifiers, are implemented solely as a data processor or service provider in these scenarios, and such data is not used by NEOGOV for its own commercial purposes. Our legal obligations as a processor and service provider are set out in our Customer contracts and policies.  Our Customers, and not us, decide what types of personal data to collect to manage their relationships with you. For example, a Customer may choose to enable collection of biometric or precise location data for its employees using our time and attendance product. We process such data only at the direction of that Customer and do not use it for our own purposes. Further, if you apply to a job or your employer utilizes our Services to manage their relationship with you, the personal data collected about you is generally controlled by the employer (our Customer). This Policy does not describe the processing of your personal data by our Customers, and we encourage you to visit the Customer’s privacy policy for information about their privacy practices. For example, if you applied to a job at a local state agency, you should contact that agency with any questions you may have relating to the personal data processing by that state agency within our Services. Where we serve as a data processor or service provider, our Customer contracts and policies require us to either instruct you to contact our Customer, or redirect your inquiry to our Customer. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. In this Section we set out general categories of personal data we may collect and the purpose for using your personal data, including the personal data collected and processed over the past year. We collect and process personal data to provide you the Services, fulfill our contractual responsibility to deliver the Services to our Customers, fulfill your requests, and pursue our legitimate interests and our business and commercial purposes. We also automatically collect data during your usage of the Services and collect other personal data about you from other sources. Your personal data will only be collected and used for purposes stated herein, where you provide additional consent, or as required by law or regulation - including national security or law enforcement requirements. Information Provided by You. We collect personal data from you directly when you visit our Services from either your computer, mobile phone, or other device, attend one our events, or communicate with our personnel. The categories of personal data we collect from you, involve the following: Types of Personal Data Why the Personal Data is collected Identification, account, and contact data, including your name, username and password, professional or personal email address, professional or personal telephone phone number, and account preferences. Create your account, perform and manage our relationship with you and our Customers, and facilitate the relationship between you and our Customers for their hiring and employment purposes. Communicate with you and send you information as part of the Services regarding your questions, comments, requests for information, contests you entered into, upcoming events, newsletters and surveys, technical notices, securi